      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-240517",
      ":question/problem": "The line $CD^(\u27f7)$ is the perpendicular bisector of $AB^(\u2015)$, and $C$ a point on the segment $AB^(\u2015)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The segments $AD^(\u2015)$ and $BD^(\u2015)$ are congruent*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of this statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $m\u2220DCB = 90^{\u2218}$ | Definition of perpendicular lines |\n| 2 | $m\u2220DCA = 90^{\u2218}$ | Definition of perpendicular lines |\n| 3 | $m\u2220DCA = m\u2220DCB$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 4 | $\u2220DCA\u2245\u2220DCB$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 5 | $AC^(\u2015)\u2245CB^(\u2015)$ | Definition of perpendicular bisector |\n| 6 | $CD^(\u2015)\u2245CD^(\u2015)$ | Reflexive property of congruence |\n| 7 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 8 | $AD^(\u2015)\u2245BD^(\u2015)$ | {{field-4}} |"
    },
